  "translations": {
    "translations": [
      {
        "iso_3166_1": "DE",
        "iso_639_1": "de",
        "name": "Deutsch",
        "english_name": "German",
        "data": {
          "homepage": "https://badische-revolution.de/",
          "overview": "Im September 1847 stellte das Volk im Offenburger Gasthaus „Salmen“ 13 Forderungen: Pressefreiheit, Schwurgerichte, eine gerechte Besteuerung und eine Volksvertretung. Was als Protest begann, wurde zur Revolution in Baden. Friedrich Hecker zog im April 1848 mit Freischärlern von Konstanz los, Gustav Struve rief im September in Lörrach die Republik aus, und im Mai 1849 lief das badische Militär zum Volk über. Großherzog Leopold floh, eine provisorische Regierung übernahm das Land. Erst preußische Truppen beendeten die Badische Revolution: Am 23. Juli 1849 kapitulierte die Festung Rastatt.",
          "runtime": 154,
          "tagline": "Die Geschichte, die wir einst vergessen sollten.",
          "title": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "iso_3166_1": "US",
        "iso_639_1": "en",
        "name": "English",
        "english_name": "English",
        "data": {
          "homepage": "",
          "overview": "In September 1847, the people gathered at the “Salmen” inn in Offenburg and put forward 13 demands: freedom of the press, trial by jury, fair taxation and a parliament representing the people. What began as a protest became the revolution in Baden. In April 1848, Friedrich Hecker set out from Konstanz with a volunteer militia, in September Gustav Struve proclaimed the republic in Lörrach, and in May 1849 the Baden army went over to the people. Grand Duke Leopold fled and a provisional government took control of the country. Only Prussian troops brought the Baden Revolution to an end: on 23 July 1849, the fortress of Rastatt surrendered.",
          "runtime": 0,
          "tagline": "The story we were once meant to forget.",
          "title": ""
        }
      }
    ]
  },
